# GitHub Actions Configuration

This project uses GitHub Actions for automated documentation validation and deployment.

## Workflow Files

### `.github/workflows/readme-checker.yml`

Validates the main README files to ensure they meet project standards:

```yaml
name: README Checker

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]
  schedule:
    - cron: '0 */6 * * *'  # Run every 6 hours

jobs:
  readme-validator:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    
    steps:
    - name: Checkout repository
      uses: actions/checkout@v4
      
    - name: Set up Node.js
      uses: actions/setup-node@v4
      with:
        node-version: '18'
        
    - name: Install markdown-validator
      run: |
        npm install -g markdown-validator
        
    - name: Validate README.md
      run: |
        markdown-validator README.md \
          --title "Main README" \
          --max-line-length 100 \
          --min-heading-level 1 \
          --max-heading-level 6 \
          --require-table-of-contents \
          --require-bibliography
          
    - name: Validate fa/README.md
      run: |
        markdown-validator fa/README.md \
          --title "Persian README" \
          --max-line-length 100 \
          --min-heading-level 1 \
          --max-heading-level 6 \
          --require-table-of-contents
          
    - name: Validate CONTRIBUTING.md
      run: |
        markdown-validator CONTRIBUTING.md \
          --title "Contributing Guide" \
          --max-line-length 100 \
          --min-heading-level 1 \
          --max-heading-level 6
```

### `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml`

Deploys documentation to GitHub Pages:

```yaml
name: Deploy to GitHub Pages

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, closed]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
    
    steps:
    - name: Checkout repository
      uses: actions/checkout@v4
      
    - name: Set up Node.js
      uses: actions/setup-node@v4
      with:
        node-version: '18'
        
    - name: Install dependencies
      run: |
        npm install -g @vuepress/cli
        npm install -g markdown-validator
        
    - name: Validate documentation
      run: |
        markdown-validator README.md fa/README.md CONTRIBUTING.md \
          --title "Documentation Validation" \
          --max-line-length 100 \
          --min-heading-level 1 \
          --max-heading-level 6
          
    - name: Build VuePress site
      run: |
        # Create VuePress config
        mkdir -p .vuepress
        cat > .vuepress/config.js << EOF
        module.exports = {
          title: 'Bore Secure Server Documentation',
          description: 'Comprehensive documentation for Bore tunneling tool',
          themeConfig: {
            nav: [
              { text: 'Home', link: '/' },
              { text: 'Installation', link: '/installation/' },
              { text: 'Configuration', link: '/configuration/' },
              { text: 'Usage', link: '/usage/' },
              { text: 'Troubleshooting', link: '/troubleshooting/' },
              { text: 'Persian Version', link: '/fa/' },
            ],
            sidebar: {
              '/installation/': [
                {
                  title: 'Installation',
                  collapsable: false,
                  children: [
                    '/installation/',
                    '/installation/linux-install',
                    '/installation/windows-install',
                    '/installation/mac-install',
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
        EOF
        
    - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages
      uses: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3
      with:
        github_token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
        publish_dir: ./.vuepress/public
        keep_files: true
        
    - name: Notify on failure
      if: failure()
      uses: actions/github-script@v6
      with:
        script: |
          github.rest.issues.create({
            owner: context.repo.owner,
            repo: context.repo.repo,
            title: `Documentation Build Failed - ${context.workflow}`,            body: `The documentation build has failed.
            
            Workflow: ${context.workflow}
            Run ID: ${context.runId}
            Commit: ${context.sha}
            
            [View the workflow run](https://github.com/${process.env.GITHUB_REPOSITORY}/actions/runs/${process.env.GITHUB_RUN_ID})
            `,
            labels: ['deployment', 'failed']
          })
```

